100000 identical diodes in parallel behind 100 ohm, 51-point source sweep
* bench.id: perf_scal_parallel_diodes_dc_n100000
* bench.group: performance
* bench.title: 100000 identical diodes in parallel behind 100 ohm, 51-point source sweep
* bench.probes: v(a), i(v1)
* bench.tol.rel: 1e-6
* bench.tol.abs: 1e-9
* bench.expect: match
* bench.ng.solver: both
* bench.timing: yes
* bench.size: 100000
* bench.est_rss_mib: 370
* bench.tags: nonlinear, dc, sweep, diode, jit_tier, devcount, family:perf_scal_parallel_diodes_dc
* bench.note: N=1e5 identical diodes (1.4 MB of deck text, 3-unknown matrix): isolates the structure-of-arrays device kernels from the matrix size; mpmath oracle: rustspice max error 4.5e-11 V (the engine's dense dc_nonlinear oracle does not converge at this N, merit 8.6e-13, so no bench.oracle is set); measured on an idle core: rustspice e2e 1.49 s (solve 1.40 s, VmHWM 79 MiB) vs ngspice SPARSE 3.35 s and KLU 3.55 s (265 and 290 MiB); over the family the solve-only exponent in N is 1.13 for rustspice and 1.23 for ngspice
.model dm D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
